3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Guillotine_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Hack Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a barre behind you bras tendus and vos pieds at épaule width. Conseil : A épaule width grip is best with the palms of vos mains facing back. You can use poignet wraps for cet exercice for a better grip. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping votre tête and eyes up and back straight, squat until your upper cuisses are parallèle au sol. Inspirez as you Lentement, go down.
3. Pressing mainly with the heel of the foot and squeezing the cuisses, go back up as you Expirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Hack_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Hip Thrust', 'Fessiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin seated on the ground with a banc directly behind you. Have a loaded barre over vos jambes. Using a fat bar or having a pad on the bar can greatly reduce the discomfort caused by cet exercice.
2. Roll the bar so that it is directly above your hanches, and lean back against the banc so that your omoplates are near the top of it.
3. Begin le mouvement by driving through vos pieds, extending your hanches vertically through the bar. Your poids should be supported by your omoplates and vos pieds. Extend as far as possible, then reverse the motion to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Hip_Thrust/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Incline Bench Press - Medium Grip', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on an incline banc. Using a medium-width grip (a grip that creates a angle de 90 degrés in the middle of le mouvement between the forearms and the upper arms), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on you upper poitrine.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, squeeze your poitrine, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : it should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Incline_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Incline Shoulder Raise', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on an Incline banc. Using a prise moyenne (a grip that is slightly wider than épaule width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping the arms straight, lift the bar by protracting your omoplates, raising the épaules from the banc as you Expirez.
3. Bring back the bar to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Incline_Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Lunge', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack just below épaule level. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and step forward with your right leg and squat down through your hanches, while keeping the torse upright and maintaining balance. Inspirez as you go down. Note: Do not allow your genou to go forward beyond your toes as you come down, as this will put undue stress on the genou joint. li>
4. Using mainly the heel of your foot, push up and go back to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. Répétez le mouvement for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform with the left leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Lunge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Rear Delt Row', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a barre using a wide (higher than épaule width) and overhand (paumes vers votre corps) grip.
2. Bend genous slightly and bend over as you keep the natural arch of votre dos. Let the arms hang in front of you as they hold the bar. Once your torse is parallèle au sol, flare the coudes out and away from votre corps. Conseil : Your torse and vos bras should resemble the letter "T". Now you are ready to begin the exercise.
3. While keeping the upper arms perpendiculaire à the torse, pull the barre up towards your upper poitrine as you squeeze the rear delts and you Expirez. Conseil : When performed correctly, cet exercice should resemble a banc press in reverse. Also, refrain from using your biceps to do the work. Focus on targeting the rear delts; the arms should only act as hooks.
4. Lentement, go back to the initial position as you Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Rear_Delt_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Rollout from Bench', 'Abdominaux', 'Barre', '1. Place a loaded barre on the ground, near the end of a banc. Kneel with both legs on the banc, and take a medium to prise serrée on the barre. C''est votre position de départ.
2. To begin, extend through the hanches to Lentement, roll the bar forward. As you roll out, flex the épaule to roll the bar above votre tête. Ensure that vos bras remain extended throughout le mouvement.
3. When the bar has been moved as far forward as possible, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Rollout_from_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Seated Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Barre', '1. Place a block about 12 inches in front of a flat banc.
2. Sit on the banc and place the ball of vos pieds on the block.
3. Have someone place a barre over your upper cuisses about 3 inches above your genous and hold it there. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Raise up on your toes as high as possible as you squeeze the mollets and as you Expirez.
5. After a second contraction, Lentement, go back to the position de départ. Conseil : To get maximum benefit stretch your mollets as far as you can.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Seated_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with back support in a squat rack. Position a barre at a height that is just above votre tête. Grab the barre with a pronated grip (paumes vers l''avant).
2. Once you pick up the barre with the correct grip width, lift the bar up over votre tête by locking vos bras. Hold at about épaule level and slightly in front of votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lower the bar down to the épaules Lentement, as you inspirez.
4. Lift the bar back up to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds at épaule width as you hold a barre with both hands in front of you using a pronated grip (paumes vers the cuisses). Conseil : vos mains should be a little wider than épaule width apart. You can use poignet wraps for cet exercice for a better grip. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Raise your épaules up as far as you can go as you Expirez and hold the contraction for a second. Conseil : Refrain from trying to lift the barre by using your biceps.
3. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Shrug Behind The Back', 'Trapèzes', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds at épaule width as you hold a barre with both hands behind votre dos using a pronated grip (paumes vers back). Conseil : vos mains should be a little wider than épaule width apart. You can use poignet wraps for cet exercice for better grip. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Raise your épaules up as far as you can go as you Expirez and hold the contraction for a second. Conseil : Refrain from trying to lift the barre by using your biceps. The arms should remain stretched out en permanence.
3. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Shrug_Behind_The_Back/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Side Bend', 'Abdominaux', 'Barre', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a barre placed on the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck). vos pieds should be épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping votre dos straight and votre tête up, bend only at the waist to the right as far as possible. Inspirez as you bend to the side. Then Maintenez la position 1 seconde and come back up to the position de départ as you expirez. Conseil : Keep the rest of the body stationary.
3. Now Répétez le mouvement but bending to the left instead. Maintenez la position 1 seconde and come back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Side_Bend/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Side Split Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a barre placed on the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck). vos pieds should be placed wide apart with the foot of the lead leg angled out to the side. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lower votre corps towards the side of your angled foot by bending the genou and hanche of your lead leg and while keeping the opposite leg only slightly bent. Inspirez as you lower votre corps.
3. Revenez en position de départ by extending the hanche and genou of the lead leg. Expirez as you perform this movement.
4. After performing the recommended amount of reps, Répétez le mouvement with the opposite leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Side_Split_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack to just below épaule level. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous and hanches as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Squat To A Bench', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first place a flat banc or a box behind you. The flat banc is used to teach you to set your hanches back and to hit depth.
2. 
3. Then, set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
4. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
5. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).
6. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous and sitting your hanches back as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until you slightly touch the banc behind you. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
7. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs and extend the hanches to go back to the position de départ.
8. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Squat_To_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Step Ups', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a barre placed on the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) and Levez-vousright behind an elevated platform (such as the one used for spotting behind a flat banc). C''est votre position de départ.
2. Place the right foot on the elevated platform. Step on the platform by extending the hanche and the genou of your right leg. Use the heel mainly to lift the rest of votre corps up and place the foot of the left leg on the platform as well. Expirez as you execute the force required to come up.
3. Step down with the left leg by flexing the hanche and genou of the right leg as you inspirez. Return to the original standing position by placing the right foot of to next to the left foot on the initial position.
4. Répétez with the right leg for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform with the left leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Step_Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Barbell Walking Lunge', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin standing with vos pieds épaule width apart and a barre across your upper back.
2. Step forward with one leg, flexing the genous to drop your hanches. Descend until your rear genou nearly touches the ground. Your posture should remain upright, and your front genou should stay above the front foot.
3. Drive through the heel of your lead foot and extend both genous to raise yourself back up.
4. Step forward with your rear foot, Répétezing the lunge on the opposite leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Barbell_Walking_Lunge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Battling Ropes', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. For cet exercice you will need a heavy rope anchored at its center 15-20 feet away. Standing in front of the rope, take an end in each hand with vos bras extended at your side. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate le mouvement by rapidly raising one arm to épaule level as quickly as you can.
3. As you let that arm drop to the position de départ, raise the opposite side.
4. Continue alternating your left and right arms, whipping the ropes up and down as fast as you can.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Battling_Ropes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bear Crawl Sled Drags', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Wearing either a harness or a loose poids belt, attach the chain to the back so that you will be facing away from the sled. Bend down so that vos mains are on the ground. votre dos should be flat and genous bent. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by driving with legs, alternating left and right. Use vos mains to maintain balance and to help pull. Try to keep votre dos flat as you move over a given distance.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bear_Crawl_Sled_Drags/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Behind Head Chest Stretch', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Sit upright on le sol with your partner behind you.
2. Place vos mains behind your hand, and push your coudes back as far as you can. Your partner should hold your coudes. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Gently attempt to pull your coudes forward with vos mains still behind votre tête for 10 or more seconds. Your partner should prevent your coudes from moving.
4. Now, relax your muscles and have your partner gently pull the coudes back as far as it comfortable for you. Be sure to let your partner know when the stretch is adequate to prevent overstretching or injury.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Behind_Head_Chest_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bench Dips', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. For cet exercice you will need to place a banc behind votre dos. With the banc perpendiculaire à votre corps, and while looking away from it, hold on to the banc on its edge with the hands fully extended, separated at épaule width. The legs will be extended forward, bent at the waist and perpendiculaire à your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lentement, lower votre corps as you inspirez by bending at the coudes until you lower yourself far enough to where there is an angle slightly smaller than 90 degrees between the upper arm and the forearm. Conseil : Keep the coudes as close as possible throughout le mouvement. Forearms should always be pointing down.
3. Using your triceps to bring your torse up again, lift yourself back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bench_Dips/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bench Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin with a box or banc 1-2 feet in front of you. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Perform a short squat in preparation for the jump; swing vos bras behind you.
3. Rebound out of this position, extending through the hanches, genous, and chevilles to jump as high as possible. Swing vos bras forward and up.
4. Jump over the banc, landing with the genous bent, absorbing the impact through the legs.
5. Turn around and face the opposite direction, then jump back over the banc.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bench_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bench Press - Powerlifting', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin by lying on the banc, getting votre tête beyond the bar if possible. Tuck vos pieds underneath you and arch votre dos. Using the bar to help support your poids, lift your épaule off the banc and retract them, squeezing the omoplates together. Use vos pieds to drive your traps into the banc. Maintain this tight body position throughout le mouvement.
2. However wide your grip, it should cover the ring on the bar. Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your épaules. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart.
3. Lower the bar to your lower poitrine or upper stomach. The bar, poignet, and coude should stay in line en permanence.
4. Pause when the barre touches your torse, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The coudes should be tucked in until lockout.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bench_Press_-_Powerlifting/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bench Press - With Bands', 'Pectoraux', 'Élastique', '1. Using a flat banc secure a band under the leg of the banc that is nearest to votre tête.
2. Once the band is secure, grab it by both handles and lie down on the banc.
3. Extend vos bras so that you are holding the band handles in front of you at épaule width.
4. Once at épaule width, rotate your poignets forward so that the palms of vos mains are facing away from you. C''est votre position de départ.
5. Bring down the handles Lentement, until your coude forms a angle de 90 degrés. Keep full control en permanence.
6. As you Expirez, bring the handles up using your pectoral muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, squeeze your poitrine, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down slowly. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
7. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bench_Press_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bench Press with Chains', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Adjust the leader chain, shortening it to the desired length.Place the chains on the sleeves of the bar.
2. Lying on the banc, get votre tête beyond the bar if possible. Tuck vos pieds underneath you and arch votre dos. Using the bar to help support your poids, lift your épaule off the banc and retract them, squeezing the omoplates together. Use vos pieds to drive your traps into the banc. Maintain this tight body position throughout le mouvement. However wide your grip, it should cover the ring on the bar.
3. Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your épaules. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart. Lower the bar to your lower poitrine or upper stomach. The bar, poignet, and coude should stay in line en permanence.
4. Pause when the barre touches your torse, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The coudes should be tucked in until lockout.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bench_Press_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bench Sprint', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand on the ground with one foot resting on a banc or box with your heel close to the edge.
2. Push off with your foot on top of the banc, extending through the hanche and genou.
3. Land with the opposite foot on top of the box, returning your other foot back to the start position.
4. Continue alternating from one foot to another to complete the set.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bench_Sprint/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent-Arm Barbell Pullover', 'Dos', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a barre using a épaule grip width.
2. Hold the bar straight over your poitrine with a bend in vos bras. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While keeping vos bras in the bent arm position, lower the poids Lentement, in an arc behind votre tête while breathing in until you feel a stretch on the poitrine.
4. At that point, bring the barre back to the position de départ using the arc through which the poids was lowered and expirez as you perform this movement.
5. Hold the poids on the initial position for a second and Répétez the motion for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent-Arm_Barbell_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent-Arm Dumbbell Pullover', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Place a haltère standing up on a flat banc.
2. Ensuring that the haltère stays securely placed at the top of the banc, lie perpendiculaire à the banc (torse across it as in forming a cross) with only your épaules lying on the surface. hanches should be below the banc and legs bent with feet firmly on le sol. The head will be off the banc as well.
3. Grasp the haltère with both hands and hold it straight over your poitrine with a bend in vos bras. Both palms should be pressing against the underside one of the sides of the haltère. C''est votre position de départ. Caution: Always ensure that the haltère used for cet exercice is secure. Using a haltère with loose plates can result in the haltère falling apart and falling on your face.
4. While keeping vos bras locked in the bent arm position, lower the poids Lentement, in an arc behind votre tête while breathing in until you feel a stretch on the poitrine.
5. At that point, bring the haltère back to the position de départ using the arc through which the poids was lowered and expirez as you perform this movement.
6. Hold the poids on the initial position for a second and Répétez the motion for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent-Arm_Dumbbell_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent-Knee Hip Raise', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Lay flat on le sol with vos bras next to your sides.
2. Now bend your genous at around a angle de 75 degrés and lift vos pieds off le sol by around 2 inches.
3. Using your lower abdominaux, bring your genous in towards you as you maintain the angle de 75 degrés bend in vos jambes. Continue this movement until you raise your hanches off of le sol by rolling your pelvis backward. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : At the end of le mouvement your genous will be over your poitrine.
4. Squeeze your abdominaux at the top of le mouvement for a second and then Revenez en position de départ Lentement, as you Inspirez. Conseil : Maintain a controlled motion en permanence.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent-Knee_Hip_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over Barbell Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Holding a barre with a pronated grip (paumes vers down), bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Conseil : Make sure that you keep the head up. The barre should hang directly in front of you as vos bras hang perpendiculaire à le sol and your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now, while keeping the torse stationary, Expirez and lift the barre to you. Keep the coudes close to the body and only use the forearms to hold the poids. At the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and hold for a brief pause.
3. Then inspirez and Lentement, lower the barre back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Barbell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over Dumbbell Rear Delt Raise With Head On Bench', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a haltère in each hand and with an incline banc in front of you.
2. While keeping votre dos straight and maintaining the natural arch of votre dos, lean forward until your forehead touches the banc in front of you. Let the arms hang in front of you perpendiculaire à the ground. The palms of vos mains should be facing each other and your torse should be parallèle au sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping your torse forward and stationary, and the arms straight with a slight bend at the coudes, lift the haltères straight to the side until both arms are parallèle au sol. Expirez as you lift the poids. Caution: avoid swinging the torse or bringing the arms back as opposed to the side.
4. After a one second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the haltères back to the position de départ.
5. Répétez the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Dumbbell_Rear_Delt_Raise_With_Head_On_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over Low-Pulley Side Lateral', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Select a poids and hold the handle of the low pulley with your right hand.
2. Bend at the waist until your torse is nearly parallèle au sol. vos jambes should be slightly bent with your left hand placed on your lower left cuisse. Your right arm should be hanging from your épaule in front of you and with a slight bend at the coude. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Raise your right arm, coude slightly bent, to the side until the arm is parallèle au sol and in line with your right ear. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. Lentement, lower the poids back to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and Répétez le mouvement with the other arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Low-Pulley_Side_Lateral/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over One-Arm Long Bar Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Put poids on one of the ends of an Olympic barre. Make sure that you either place the other end of the barre in the corner of two walls; or put a heavy object on the ground so the barre cannot slide backward.
2. Bend forward until your torse is as close to parallel with le sol as you can and keep your genous slightly bent.
3. Now grab the bar with one arm just behind the plates on the side where the poids was placed and put your other hand on your genou. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Pull the bar straight up with your coude in (to maximize back stimulation) until the plates touch your lower poitrine. Squeeze the back muscles as you lift the poids up and Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the top of le mouvement. Expirez as you lift the poids. Conseil : Do not allow for any swinging of the torse. Only the arm should move.
5. Lentement, lower the bar to the position de départ getting a nice stretch on the lats. Conseil : Do not let the plates touch le sol. To ensure the best range of motion, I recommend using small plates (25-lb ones) as opposed to larger plates (like 35-45lb ones).
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and switch arms.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_One-Arm_Long_Bar_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over Two-Arm Long Bar Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Put poids on one of the ends of an Olympic barre. Make sure that you either place the other end of the barre in the corner of two walls; or put a heavy object on the ground so the barre cannot slide backward.
2. Bend forward until your torse is as close to parallel with le sol as you can and keep your genous slightly bent.
3. Now grab the bar with both arms just behind the plates on the side where the poids was placed and put your other hand on your genou. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Pull the bar straight up with your coudes in (to maximize back stimulation) until the plates touch your lower poitrine. Squeeze the back muscles as you lift the poids up and Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the top of le mouvement. Expirez as you lift the poids. Conseil : Use a stirrup or double handle cable attachment by hooking it under the end of the bar.
5. Lentement, lower the bar to the position de départ getting a nice stretch on the lats. Conseil : Do not let the plates touch le sol. To ensure the best range of motion, I recommend using small plates (25-lb ones) as opposed to larger plates (like 35-45lb ones).
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Arm_Long_Bar_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over Two-Dumbbell Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Haltères', '1. With a haltère in each hand (paumes vers your torse), bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward by bending at the waist; as you bend make sure to keep votre dos straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Conseil : Make sure that you keep the head up. The poids should hang directly in front of you as vos bras hang perpendiculaire à le sol and your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping the torse stationary, lift the haltères to your side (as you Expirez), keeping the coudes close to the body (do not exert any force with the forearm other than holding the poids). On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
3. Lentement, lower the poids again to the position de départ as you inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Dumbbell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Over Two-Dumbbell Row With Palms In', 'Milieu du dos', 'Haltères', '1. With a haltère in each hand (paumes vers each other), bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Conseil : Make sure that you keep the head up. The poids should hang directly in front of you as vos bras hang perpendiculaire à le sol and your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping the torse stationary, lift the haltères to your side as you Expirez, squeezing your omoplates together. On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
3. Lentement, lower the poids again to the position de départ as you inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Dumbbell_Row_With_Palms_In/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bent Press', 'Abdominaux', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean a kettlebell to your épaule. Clean the kettlebell to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you raise the kettlebell towards your épaule. The poignet should rotate as you do so. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin my leaning to the side opposite the kettlebell, continuing until you are able to touch the ground with your free hand, keeping your eyes on the kettlebell. As you do so, press the poids vertically be extending through the coude, keeping your arm perpendiculaire à the ground.
3. Return to an upright position, with the kettlebell above votre tête. Return the kettlebell to the épaule and Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bent_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bicycling', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. To begin, seat yourself on the bike and adjust the seat to your height.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bicycling/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bicycling, Stationary', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, seat yourself on the bike and adjust the seat to your height.
2. Select the desired option from the menu. You may have to start pedaling to turn it on. You can use the manual setting, or you can select a program to use. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. The level of resistance can be changed throughout the workout. The handles can be used to monitor your heart rate to help you stay at an appropriate intensity.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bicycling_Stationary/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Board Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin by lying on the banc, getting votre tête beyond the bar if possible. One to five boards, made out of 2x6''s, can be screwed together and held in place by a training partner, bands, or just tucked under your shirt.
2. Tuck vos pieds underneath you and arch votre dos. Using the bar to help support your poids, lift your épaule off the banc and retract them, squeezing the omoplates together. Use vos pieds to drive your traps into the banc. Maintain this tight body position throughout le mouvement.
3. You can take a standard banc grip, or épaule width to focus on the triceps. Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your épaules. The bar, poignet, and coude should stay in line en permanence. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart.
4. Lower the bar to the boards, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The coudes should be tucked in until lockout.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Board_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Body-Up', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Assume a plank position on the ground. You should be supporting your bodyweight on your toes and forearms, keeping your torse straight. Your forearms should be épaule-width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Pressing your palms firmly into the ground, extend through the coudes to raise votre corps from the ground. Keep your torse rigid as you perform le mouvement.
3. Lentement, lower your forearms back to the ground by allowing the coudes to flex.
4. Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Body-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Body Tricep Press', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Position a bar in a rack at poitrine height.
2. Standing, take a épaule width grip on the bar and step a yard or two back, feet together and arms extended so that you are leaning on the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by flexing the coude, lowering yourself towards the bar.
4. Pause, and then reverse the motion by extending the coudes.
5. Progress from bodyweight by adding chains over your épaules.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Body_Tricep_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bodyweight Flyes', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre EZ', '1. Position two equally loaded EZ bars on the ground next to each other. Ensure they are able to roll.
2. Assume a push-up position over the bars, supporting your poids on your toes and hands with vos bras extended and body straight.
3. Place vos mains on the bars. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Using a slow and controlled motion, move vos mains away from the midline of votre corps, rolling the bars apart. Inspirez during this portion of the motion.
5. After moving the bars as far apart as you can, Revenez en position de départ by pulling them back together. Expirez as you perform this movement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bodyweight Mid Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Begin by taking a medium to prise large on a pull-up apparatus with your paumes vers away from you. From a hanging position, tuck your genous to your poitrine, leaning back and getting vos jambes over your side of the pull-up apparatus. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Beginning with vos bras straight, flex the coudes and retract the omoplates to raise votre corps up until vos jambes contact the pull-up apparatus.
3. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Mid_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bodyweight Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds épaule width apart. You can place vos mains behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin le mouvement by flexing your genous and hanches, sitting back with your hanches.
3. Continue down to full depth if you are able,and quickly reverse the motion until you Revenez en position de départ. As you squat, keep votre tête and poitrine up and push your genous out.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bodyweight Walking Lunge', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Begin standing with vos pieds épaule width apart and vos mains on your hanches.
